## Technical findings
- “Input space” maps to current `areas[]`, not `equipment[]`.
- Best fit: add area field `extractor_type`.
- User-approved enum:
  - `sencillo`
  - `ducteable`
- Do not overload `installation_type`; current meaning = physical install (`muro`, `techo`, `conducto`).
- Capacity ranges must not infer category. User says usage type, not capacity. CFM thresholds are advisory metadata/warnings only.
- Selector must filter exact category before airflow ranking.
- Multi-area equipment with mixed categories must choose `ducteable` automatically per user decision.
- Catalog JSON can stay flat but needs model category + image/provenance fields.
- User-approved image policy: two local category images only, not per-model URL runtime.

## Risks
- Strict schema will break fixtures unless all input/docs/examples updated.
- Field-name drift risk: freeze `extractor_type` across input/catalog/spec/memory.
- Existing skill tests won’t catch selector regressions.
- Web image URLs can violate offline/local-output policy unless stored only as provenance.
- Missing catalog assets become blockers if image validation strict; use 2 category images.

## Recommendation for planning
- Add required `areas[].extractor_type` enum: `sencillo`, `ducteable`.
- Derive per-equipment `extractor_type` from served areas in spec runner.
- If served area types mixed, choose `ducteable` automatically.
- Add required model `extractor_type` to catalog and exact category filter to selector.
- Treat JSON as source of truth; no live web lookup in runtime.
- Use required local `image_asset` pointing to category image.
- Preserve `source_url`, `catalog_url`, `image_source_url`, `rating_basis`, `source_notes`, `retrieved_at` for provenance.
- Add category to `spec.json` constraints/model output and memory visible rendering.
- Add tests for missing category, enum validation, simple vs ductable exact selection, mixed-category ductable fallback, image policy, memory category render.

